  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/glyptoperichthys-parnaibae-2/",
      "html": "<p>Glyptoperichthys parnaibae grows to 40-50 cm in length and is probably the most beautiful of all Glyptoperichthys species.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/glyptoperichthys-parnaibae-2/",
      "html": "<p>So far known exclusively from the Rio Parnaiba in Brazil. The Rio Parnaiba is located in the northeast of Brazil and has a high proportion of endemic fish species, i.e. species occurring only there, because there is no connection to other river systems. In its distribution area the species is very common and serves as cheap food for poorer population groups.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/glyptoperichthys-parnaibae-2/",
      "html": "<p>Large aquariums are needed to keep these large fish, but otherwise Glyptoperichthys parnaibae are very easy to care for.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/glyptoperichthys-parnaibae-2/",
      "html": "<p>Investigation of the stomach content showed that this species eats not only aufwuchs, but also insect larvae.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/glyptoperichthys-parnaibae-2/",
      "html": "<p>The juveniles are, like all sailfin plecs, quite delightful fish.</p>"
    }
  ],
